jobs.description:
Are you an experienced forklift operator who feels right at home in a logistics environment? Would you like to work for a stable organization where you’ll work alongside a small, close-knit team to ensure everything runs smoothly? Then we have a great opportunity for you!

For a client in Weert, we’re looking for an experienced forklift operator who enjoys working a 3-shift schedule. You’ll be joining a large logistics company where safety, teamwork, and a pleasant work atmosphere are key priorities.

What will you be doing?

As a forklift operator, you’ll be responsible for moving goods efficiently and safely within the warehouse. You’ll spend most of your workday operating the forklift. Together with four colleagues, you’ll ensure that all pallets and goods are placed in the correct locations and that outgoing orders are ready on time.

Your duties will include:

- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Picking orders and preparing them for shipment;
- Scanning goods;
- Moving pallets and goods within the warehouse;
- Preparing outgoing orders for transport.

You'll be operating a forklift with double forks, loading from the side. Do you have experience with this? If so, be sure to read on! 

You’ve already gained considerable experience operating a forklift and understand how important it is to work safely and accurately. You’re flexible, keep a cool head during busy periods, and are comfortable working shifts.

In addition:

- You have at least 1 year of experience as a forklift operator;
- You hold a valid forklift operator’s certificate;
- You are fluent in Dutch or English;
- You are available full-time;
- You work with precision and always put safety first.

Can your colleagues in production count on spotless and hygienic workspaces? Do you enjoy staying active on the job? Then you can quickly start working as a cleaner or industrial cleaner at Luiten! Your full-time workday starts around 9:00 or 10:00 AM. You’ll change into your work attire, grab your cleaning materials and equipment, and begin moving between the various production areas with your high-pressure cleaner.
Not only will you thoroughly clean the production spaces, but you’ll also ensure that the machines used to process and package meat—and all related materials—are meticulously cleaned. You take care of your own work, following HACCP and hygiene regulations carefully. In addition to cleaning, you make sure that every area is safe to enter and ready for use.
No need for an activity tracker here, as you’ll definitely get plenty of daily movement in this role! Together with your friendly, multicultural team, you’ll ensure production can start on time and in a clean environment.

- You are available full-time from Monday till Friday;
- Overtime doesn’t wear you out—instead, it makes your wallet fuller;
- You speak Dutch or English, essential for safety on the work floor;
- Some experience with cleaning and/or sanitation is a plus.

Work in a international production team and help make high-quality products. You'll operate machines, check quality, and keep everything running smoothly. As a Production Employee, your tasks are broad and varied. While some tasks are repetitive, employees rotate weekly between different workstations and responsibilities. This ensures that you remain widely deployable, engaged, and continuously developing new skills.

What you'll do:

- Operating and monitoring production machines;
- Performing quality checks and completing required documentation;
- Counting, stamping, and registering production time;
- Preparing finished products and orders for shipping;
- Keeping your workspace clean, organized, and safe;
- Reporting deviations, malfunctions, or quality issues to your team leader.

You will work in three shifts:

- 06:00 – 14:00
- 14:00 – 22:00
- 22:00 – 06:00

- Good knowledge of the English language;
- Ability to work accurately and precisely – this is the most important requirement;
- Basic computer skills (data entry, forms, registrations);
- A focused mindset with the ability to work quickly and efficiently;
- Flexibility and willingness to learn and rotate between workstations;
- Availability and motivation to work in a 3- as well as a 2-shift system;

What will you do?

As an Operator, you will work in a dynamic production environment within the fresh produce industry (potatoes, vegetables, and fruit). You will play an important role in the sorting process of avocados and mangoes, ensuring that production runs smoothly and efficiently.

During your first week, you will work on the sorting line to gain a thorough understanding of the production process. You will sort fruit based on its ripeness while learning how the sorting department operates. After this onboarding period, you will be paired with an experienced buddy who will guide and support you until you are confident enough to work independently.

Your responsibilities include:

- Working on the sorting line during your onboarding period, sorting fruit based on ripeness;
- Receiving and processing production orders using the computer;
- Translating production orders into clear instructions for the sorting team;
- Supervising a sorting line of approximately 7 employees;
- Monitoring the quality and progress of the production process.

This is a varied role in which you will combine hands-on production work with team leadership. You will continuously switch between planning, execution, and coordinating your team to ensure production targets are met.

Working Days & Hours

You will work 38 hours per week, Monday through Friday, with occasional Saturdays when required.

Working hours: 06:45 AM – 03:30 PM, with occasional overtime until production has been completed.

- Available to work 38 hours per week, Monday through Friday (occasional Saturdays);
- Comfortable working with computers;
- Good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Experience in the fresh produce industry is an advantage;
- Experience as an Operator or in a supervisory role;
- Able to lead and motivate a team;
- Stress-resistant and able to adapt to changing circumstances.
